✅ QUESTION 5: MAXIMUM SUM RECTANGLE IN A 2D MATRIX

(Kadane’s Algorithm + Matrix Compression)

This problem looks scary at first, but once you see the trick, it becomes elegant 😌

📌 Problem Statement

You are given a 2D matrix of integers (can include negative numbers).

Find the submatrix (rectangle) with the maximum sum and return that sum.

👉 A submatrix is defined by:

Left column

Right column

Top row

Bottom row

💡 Key Insight

Direct brute force is O(n⁶) ❌

Optimize it using:

Column compression

1D Kadane’s Algorithm

👉 We fix left & right columns, compress rows into a 1D array, then apply Kadane.

🧠 Algorithm Steps

Fix a left column L

Create an array temp[] of size rows, initialize with 0

For each right column R ≥ L:

Add column R values into temp[]

Apply Kadane’s Algorithm on temp[]

Track maximum sum

Repeat for all column pairs

⏱ Time & Space Complexity

Time: O(cols² × rows)

Space: O(rows)

☕ Java Code
public class MaximumSumRectangle {

    static int kadane(int[] arr) {
        int maxSoFar = arr[0];
        int currMax = arr[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
            currMax = Math.max(arr[i], currMax + arr[i]);
            maxSoFar = Math.max(maxSoFar, currMax);
        }
        return maxSoFar;
    }

    static int maxSumRectangle(int[][] matrix) {

        int rows = matrix.length;
        int cols = matrix[0].length;
        int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for (int left = 0; left < cols; left++) {

            int[] temp = new int[rows];

            for (int right = left; right < cols; right++) {

                for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++)
                    temp[i] += matrix[i][right];

                int currentSum = kadane(temp);
                maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, currentSum);
            }
        }
        return maxSum;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[][] matrix = {
            { 1,  2, -1, -4, -20},
            {-8, -3,  4,  2,   1},
            { 3,  8, 10,  1,   3},
            {-4, -1,  1,  7,  -6}
        };

        System.out.println(maxSumRectangle(matrix));
    }
}

🧩 Line-by-Line Explanation
🔹 Kadane’s Algorithm
currMax = Math.max(arr[i], currMax + arr[i]);


Decides whether to:

Start new subarray

Or extend existing one

🔹 Fix Left Column
for (int left = 0; left < cols; left++)


Defines starting column of rectangle.

🔹 Compress Columns
temp[i] += matrix[i][right];


Transforms 2D matrix → 1D array (row sums).

🔹 Apply Kadane
int currentSum = kadane(temp);


Finds best top & bottom row for current column range.

🔍 Example Walkthrough (Key Part)

For:

Left = 1, Right = 3


Compressed temp:

Row wise sum → [ -3, 3, 19, 7 ]


Applying Kadane:

Max subarray = 3 + 19 + 7 = 29


This corresponds to rectangle:

-3   4   2
 8  10   1
-1   1   7

